cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Christian Thinkers Writers
message: If you use this corpus, please cite it.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Phoenix
    website: https://github.com/eulestadt
repository-code: https://github.com/eulestadt/christian-thinkers-writers
url: https://github.com/eulestadt/christian-thinkers-writers
abstract: >-
  Public archival corpus for Christian Thinkers Writers: a Wikipedia
  Category:Christian writers census, closed-form Hoge and Gorsuch I/E-R
  intrinsic-motivation scores on English public-domain works, and
  Constitutional AI treatment (I/E-R intrinsic top 40) versus
  citation-control (same year window, treatment authors excluded)
  datasets generated with deepseek-flash. The current fine-tune (v3)
  keeps the top 20 treatment books by ier_intrinsic, rewrites those
  traces into one weighed turn, and compares a weighted arm
  (w = s/mean, no clip), a uniform arm (w = 1 on the same rows), and
  a size-matched control. Each arm has 1,001 CAI rows plus 300
  format-replay rows (Kish ESS 789.94, max weight 2.248), trained
  with R-DPO alpha 0.01 and beta 0.1. The reported score is WiSE-FT
  lambda 0.5. UltraChat is not in the v3 mix.
keywords:
  - constitutional AI
  - intrinsic religious motivation
  - I/E-R
  - Christian writers
  - public domain
  - alignment
license: MIT
